-- title:
--   §9.2.1 — the series (9.3) is characteristic, strict, isomorphism-invariant, of length $\le\lfloor\log_2|Q|\rfloor$
-- statement:
--   Let $Q$ be a finite group and let $1=N_0,N_1,\dots$ be the series of §9.2.1: $N_{i+1}$ is the preimage of $S(Q/N_i)$, where $S(K)=\mathrm{AC}(K)$ if $\mathrm{srad}(K)\ne1$ and $S(K)=\mathrm{Soc}(K)$ otherwise. Let $\ell$ be the least index with $N_\ell=Q$. Then
--   1. $N_\ell=Q$ (the series reaches $Q$);
--   2. every $N_i$ is characteristic in $Q$;
--   3. $N_i<N_{i+1}$ for every $i<\ell$;
--   4. $\ell\le\lfloor\log_2|Q|\rfloor$;
--   5. the construction is preserved by isomorphisms: every isomorphism $\varphi:Q\to Q'$ maps $N_i(Q)$ onto $N_i(Q')$ for all $i$;
--   6. for every finite group $K$: $S(K)$ is characteristic in $K$; $S(K)\ne1$ if $K\ne1$; if $\mathrm{srad}(K)\ne1$ then $\mathrm{AC}(K)$ is a nontrivial elementary abelian $r$-group for a prime $r$; if $\mathrm{srad}(K)=1$ then $\mathrm{Soc}(K)$ is a direct product of nonabelian simple groups.
--
--   This series is the skeleton of the group isomorphism algorithm: its terms are canonical, so any isomorphism $G\to H$ respects them, and its length is logarithmic in the order.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Elementary abelian is the published `IsElementaryAbelian r` (commutative with exponent dividing $r$). The series is indexed by all natural numbers and stays at $Q$ after $\ell$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - encoding: AC(K) = {x ∈ D_r : x^r = 1} → the normal subgroup generated by {x ∈ D : x^r = 1}, D the last nonidentity derived term of srad K; reason: D is abelian and characteristic, so the set is already a normal subgroup and equals {x ∈ D_r : x^r = 1}; the closure only supplies normality
--   - encoding: "the selection is preserved by isomorphisms" → ∀ φ : Q ≃* Q', ∀ i, φ(N_i(Q)) = N_i(Q'); reason: the construction refers to nothing but the group structure
--   - encoding: ℓ, the index of the last term N_ℓ = Q → the least i with N_i = Q (`seriesLength`); reason: with strict inclusions this is the paper's ℓ
--   - reading: "every inclusion is strict"; "a nontrivial elementary abelian subgroup S(Q/N_i)" (p.95) → also stated for S itself: S(K) ≠ 1 for every nontrivial finite K, and AC(K) ≠ 1 is elementary abelian when srad(K) ≠ 1; reason: every finite K is Q/N_0 for Q = K, so this is the paper's claim at i = 0
--   - encoding: "a direct product of nonabelian simple groups" → isomorphic to a product of finitely many simple, noncommutative groups (`IsProdNonabelianSimple`); reason: standard meaning; the empty product is the trivial group
-- source:
--   Qiao, Zhang, Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order, preprint, Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), §9.2.1, (9.3), p.94 (PDF p.98); p.95 (PDF p.99)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_cfsg_elementary_abelian
import Definitions.Def_GroupIsoPoly_charSeries

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace GroupIsoPoly

/-- **§9.2.1 — the characteristic subgroup series (9.3).**

Qiao, Zhang, *Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order*, preprint,
Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), §9.2.1, p.94 (PDF p.98): "construct a series
1 = N0 < · · · < Nj = srad(Q) < · · · < Nℓ = Q (9.3) of subgroups characteristic in Q … Both choices
make S(K) characteristic in K … Thus every Ni is characteristic in the original group Q. The selection
is preserved by isomorphisms, every inclusion is strict, and ℓ ≤ ⌊log2 |Q|⌋"; p.95 (PDF p.99): "the
construction chooses a nontrivial elementary abelian subgroup S(Q/Ni)".

For every finite group `Q`, with `N_i = charSeries Q i` and `ℓ = seriesLength Q`:
1. `N_ℓ = Q`;
2. every `N_i` is characteristic in `Q`;
3. `N_i < N_{i+1}` for `i < ℓ`;
4. `ℓ ≤ ⌊log₂ |Q|⌋`;
5. every isomorphism `φ : Q ≃* Q'` maps `N_i(Q)` onto `N_i(Q')`;
6. for every finite group `K`: `S(K)` is characteristic; `S(K) ≠ 1` when `K ≠ 1`; when
   `srad(K) ≠ 1`, `AC(K)` is a nontrivial elementary abelian `r`-group for a prime `r`; when
   `srad(K) = 1`, `Soc(K)` is a direct product of nonabelian simple groups.

**Formalization Note.** Elementary abelian is the published `IsElementaryAbelian r` (commutative, of
exponent dividing `r`). -/
theorem charSeries_spec (Q : Type*) [Group Q] [Finite Q] :
    charSeries Q (seriesLength Q) = ⊤ ∧
    (∀ i, (charSeries Q i).Characteristic) ∧
    (∀ i < seriesLength Q, charSeries Q i < charSeries Q (i + 1)) ∧
    seriesLength Q ≤ Nat.log 2 (Nat.card Q) ∧
    (∀ (Q' : Type*) [Group Q'] (φ : Q ≃* Q') (i : ℕ),
      (charSeries Q i).map φ.toMonoidHom = charSeries Q' i) ∧
    (∀ (K : Type*) [Group K] [Finite K],
      (S K).Characteristic ∧ (Nontrivial K → S K ≠ ⊥) ∧
      (srad K ≠ ⊥ → AC K ≠ ⊥ ∧ ∃ r : ℕ, r.Prime ∧ IsElementaryAbelian r (AC K)) ∧
      (srad K = ⊥ → IsProdNonabelianSimple (soc K))) := by sorry

end GroupIsoPoly
